# ---------------------------------------------------------
# DeepZero Environment Configuration
# ---------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to '.env' and configure the tools you use.
# DeepZero will automatically load '.env' using python-dotenv.

# =========================================================
# 1. LLM Backend
#
# Two options - pick per pipeline via `model:` in pipeline.yaml
# (or override with `deepzero run -m ...`).
#
# a) Claude Code (no API key)
#    Uses your own locally installed, already-signed-in Claude
#    Code CLI. Install it and sign in with your own account first.
#    Both bundled pipelines use its default model; no API key is needed:
#      model: claude-code           # default model
#      model: claude-code/sonnet    # or /opus, or a full model name
#    Requires: `claude` on PATH and signed in (run `claude`).
#
#    Optional override for both bundled pipelines (or pass -m per run):
#    Uncomment at most one DEEPZERO_MODEL example.
# DEEPZERO_MODEL=claude-code
# DEEPZERO_MODEL=claude-code/opus
#
# b) LiteLLM (API key, metered)
#    Best for CI/servers. Provide keys for whatever endpoints
#    your pipelines target, e.g. model: openai/gpt-4o
#    Install the Python extra: python -m pip install -e ".[llm]"
# DEEPZERO_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o
# =========================================================
# GEMINI_API_KEY=AI...
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...
# VERTEXAI_PROJECT=
# VERTEXAI_LOCATION=

# =========================================================
# 2. GHIDRA Headless Configuration
# Required by the `ghidra_decompile` processor
# Replace these example paths with your own installation directories.
# =========================================================
# GHIDRA_INSTALL_DIR=/path/to/ghidra_11.X_PUBLIC
# JAVA_HOME=/path/to/java/jdk-17


